# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored.
# Used by Electron for TMDB TV Series sync (popular / airing / trending → Rive play)
# and EZTV TV Series sync (TMDB → EZTV by IMDb).
# Also baked into the Android/Vite build (same key name) so shelves sync on phone.
#
# Packaged desktop does not ship .env. Put the same file at:
#   F:\Jiyu\user-data\.env   (when using the F: data root)
#   or next to Jiyu.exe
#   or %APPDATA%\jiyu-media-center\.env
TMDB_API_KEY=

# Optional — Wyzie Subs softsub fallback (primary).
# Desktop Electron: WYZIE_API_KEY in this file (read by electron/main.cjs only — never Vite).
# Android / Tizen / shared web: deploy workers/jiyu-wyzie then set the public Worker URL:
#   WYZIE_PROXY_URL=https://jiyu-wyzie.<you>.workers.dev
# See workers/jiyu-wyzie/README.md. Never put WYZIE_API_KEY in Vite envPrefix / APK / wgt.
# WYZIE_API_KEY=
# WYZIE_PROXY_URL=

# Optional — OpenSubtitles softsub fallback (secondary after Wyzie).
# Free API key: https://www.opensubtitles.com/en/consumers
# Desktop: OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY in this file (Electron only).
# Android: also put the secret on the Worker: wrangler secret put OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY
# OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY=

# Optional — only needed on the machine that publishes installers to GitHub Releases
# (npm run release:win / release:linux). Not required for end users.
# Create a classic PAT with `repo` scope: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# GH_TOKEN=
